I know that spellcasting isn't really too easy; but it could be made
even harder. As it is now, there is no limit to the number of spells
you can learn, except (a) finding, understanding and transporting
spellbooks, and (b) the time factor of forgetting spells.  I think
there should be an upper limit on how many spells you can know, similar
to the skill slot system which gives an upper limit on how many weapon
types you can use.

Thoughts?



